Source: AGVN, reconstructed from Ludashi's opengl_zink.tzst (not published by Ludashi). Verified against its
libgallium-24.3.0.so (inlined dri_fill_in_modes, 0x708d50..0x709194): getenv("WRAPPER_SURFACE_FORMAT"),
strcmp with "bgra8"; "bgra8" skips pipe_formats[11..14] (RGBA8888/RGBX8888 UNORM/SRGB), any other value skips
[4..7] (BGRA8888/BGRX8888 UNORM/SRGB); the upstream loader RGBA-ordering filter is gone.
Why: the app always sets WRAPPER_SURFACE_FORMAT (GuestProgramLauncherComponent); the GL visuals must match the
Vulkan wrapper's swapchain channel order, or colours come out swapped.

